---
name: Map audit.log lines to OCSF
description: |
  Normalizes the records of one audited `execve` call. The normalizer groups
  the records by their stamp, maps the event to an OCSF Process Activity, and
  retains the source lines in `raw_data`.
---

from {line: "node=web-01.example type=SYSCALL msg=audit(1767225600.123:4521): arch=c000003e syscall=59 success=yes exit=0 a0=55d0c8a1b2c0 a1=55d0c8a1b350 a2=55d0c8a1b3a0 a3=8 items=2 ppid=812 pid=813 auid=1000 uid=1000 gid=1000 euid=1000 suid=1000 fsuid=1000 egid=1000 sgid=1000 fsgid=1000 tty=pts0 ses=3 comm=\"cat\" exe=\"/usr/bin/cat\" subj=unconfined key=\"exec\""},
  {line: "node=web-01.example type=EXECVE msg=audit(1767225600.123:4521): argc=2 a0=\"cat\" a1=\"/etc/hostname\""},
  {line: "node=web-01.example type=CWD msg=audit(1767225600.123:4521): cwd=\"/home/alice\""},
  {line: "node=web-01.example type=PATH msg=audit(1767225600.123:4521): item=0 name=\"/usr/bin/cat\" inode=1100 dev=fd:00 mode=0100755 ouid=0 ogid=0 rdev=00:00 nametype=NORMAL"},
  {line: "node=web-01.example type=PROCTITLE msg=audit(1767225600.123:4521): proctitle=636174002F6574632F686F73746E616D65"}
auditd::ocsf::normalize
this = ocsf_derive(this)
